ng scams. (Patterns: crypto airdrop scam, phishing/wallet drainer (connect wallet to claim), urgent/limited-time pressure, too-good-to-be-true free crypto payout, suspicious external link, fake transaction/success screenshot)", "Abstained": false, "CheckName": 10, "ProcessingTimeMs": 0}, {"Score": 4.9, "Details": "AI: Spam - This is a classic crypto airdrop/phishing-style solicitation: it pushes users to click an external link (canonical-spam.test/spin), claims large guaranteed rewards (5 SOL + 100,000 tokens), uses urgency/scarcity (“daily limited number, do it quickly”), and tries to disarm skepticism (“thought it was a scam but it was real”). It’s unrelated to survival/common-sense discussion and is promotional/unwanted with high scam likelihood.", "Abstained": false, "CheckName": 6, "ProcessingTimeMs": 0}]}', 0, -100026957614982, 5.9, 10.8);
